Use the LIST command to get a listing of files in the current download
directory.  Enter LIST by itself, and you will see the following:

Enter search pattern, [RETURN] for all files
or # for new files
>

If you want a complete listing of files, simply hit the RETURN key.  If
you want only new files since your last call, enter '#'.  If you have an
idea of what the name of the desired file is, enter a search pattern.  If the
letters you provide occur in the names of any files, those files will be
displayed.

As a shortcut, you may view all files via:
LIST -a     or     LIST *
Or, you can view new files via:
LIST -n     or     LIST #
Finally, you can supply a search pattern, <pattern> via:
LIST <pattern>
